# Read from the build CONTEXT root, which is the repo root for the three python
# images — apps/backend, apps/cron and apps/mcp are all built with
# `-f <path> .`, so a .dockerignore next to any of them would be ignored. The
# frontend builds from its own directory and has its own.
#
# Patterns are matched against the whole relative path, so the nested ones need
# an explicit **/ — a bare `.venv/` would only ever match one at the root, and
# every venv now lives inside apps/.
#
# data/cache alone is >100MB of scraped HTTP responses — the container refetches
# live anyway (gather always runs with the cache off), so none of it belongs in
# the build context.
data/
.git/
.env
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/

# Neither python image serves the SPA; the web service is apps/frontend's own.
apps/frontend/

# Root node_modules exists only so `railway config` can resolve railway/iac.
# No image copies it, but the context is the repo root, so it uploads without this.
node_modules/
